# Exam track — Theme: Summer — Sub-lesson 1: Vocabulary
# Sproochentest oral-exam topic. Target level ~B1 (authoring guideline only).
#
# These are the learners' real answers, gathered by interview — two speakers
# share this theme (Sergii and his wife Marie), so a few questions in
# sub-lesson 3 carry two different, both genuine answers. Do not "improve",
# merge or genericize them in a later editing pass.
#
# LOD corrections applied to the interview wording: Klimm -> d'Klimaanlag
# (Klimm is not in LOD), Schatte -> de Schiet, Melon -> d'Meloun,
# Sonnenhut -> de Sonnenhutt. Colloquial "Canicule" is kept because LOD lists
# it as a noun in its own right, glossed apart from Hëtztwell so the two entries
# stay distinguishable in word match.

@lesson J1.01 "Summer Vocabulary"

@word de Summer = the summer
@word de Wanter = the winter
@word d'Fréijoer = the spring
@word den Hierscht = the autumn
@word d'Joreszäit = the season
@word d'Joreszäiten = the seasons
@word de Mount = the month
@word d'Méint = the months
@word de Juni = June
@word de Juli = July
@word den August = August
@word de Summerdag = the summer day
@word d'Summervakanz = the summer holidays
@word d'Fräizäit = the free time
@word d'Wieder = the weather
@word d'Temperatur = the temperature
@word d'Temperaturen = the temperatures
@word de Grad = the degree
@word d'Hëtzt = the heat
@word d'Hëtztwell = the heatwave
@word d'Canicule = the hot spell
@word d'Klimaanlag = the air conditioning
@word de Ventilator = the fan
@word d'Sonn = the sun
@word de Schnéi = the snow
@word de Reen = the rain
@word d'Wollek = the cloud
@word de Wand = the wind
@word d'Loft = the air
@word de Schiet = the shade
@word d'Klima = the climate
@word d'Sonnecrème = the suncream
@word de Sonnenhutt = the sun hat
@word de Sonnebrand = the sunburn
@word d'Fënster = the window
@word waarm = warm
@word kal = cold
@word naass = wet
@word dréchen = dry
@word sonneg = sunny
@word frësch = fresh
@word dreckeg = dirty
@word héich = high
@word typesch = typical
@word reenen = to rain
@word schwammen = to swim
@word spadséieren = to go for a walk
@word trëppelen = to stroll
@word zoumaachen = to close
@word benotzen = to use
@word zwanzeg = twenty
@word fënnefanzwanzeg = twenty-five
@word véierzeg = forty
@word dräi = three

@sentence
@lu Fir mech ass de Summer eng waarm Zäit.
@en For me the summer is a warm time.
@distractor-lu Wanter
@distractor-lu kal
@distractor-en winter
@distractor-en cold

@sentence
@lu Zwanzeg bis fënnefanzwanzeg Grad si gutt fir mech.
@en Twenty to twenty-five degrees are good for me.
@distractor-lu véierzeg
@distractor-lu schlecht
@distractor-en forty
@distractor-en bad

@sentence
@lu Ech hunn et net gär, wann et ze waarm ass.
@en I do not like it when it is too warm.
@distractor-lu kal
@distractor-lu Schnéi
@distractor-en cold
@distractor-en snow

@sentence
@lu Dëse Summer hate mir dräi Hëtztwellen zu Lëtzebuerg.
@en This summer we had three heatwaves in Luxembourg.
@distractor-lu Wolleken
@distractor-lu zwanzeg
@distractor-en clouds
@distractor-en twenty

@sentence
@lu D'Temperature waren ze héich fir mäin Hond.
@en The temperatures were too high for my dog.
@distractor-lu niddreg
@distractor-lu Wand
@distractor-en low
@distractor-en wind

@sentence
@lu Ech hunn de Schnéi richteg gär.
@en I really like the snow.
@distractor-lu Reen
@distractor-lu Hëtzt
@distractor-en rain
@distractor-en heat

@sentence
@lu Am Fréijoer an am spéiden Hierscht ass et dreckeg.
@en In the spring and in the late autumn it is dirty.
@distractor-lu Summer
@distractor-lu propper
@distractor-en summer
@distractor-en clean

@sentence
@lu Ech maachen all Fënster zou, wann et ze waarm ass.
@en I close every window when it is too warm.
@distractor-lu Dier
@distractor-lu kal
@distractor-en door
@distractor-en cold

@sentence
@lu Mat der Klimaanlag war et besser fir mech.
@en With the air conditioning it was better for me.
@distractor-lu Ventilator
@distractor-lu Reen
@distractor-en fan
@distractor-en rain

@sentence
@lu Ech mengen, et ass net normal, datt de Summer sou waarm ass.
@en I think it is not normal that the summer is so warm.
@distractor-lu typesch
@distractor-lu Wanter
@distractor-en typical
@distractor-en winter

@sentence
@lu D'Loft ass moies nach frësch.
@en The air is still fresh in the morning.
@distractor-lu owes
@distractor-lu waarm
@distractor-en evening
@distractor-en warm

@sentence
@lu Am Summer ass d'Wieder zu Lëtzebuerg meeschtens gutt.
@en In the summer the weather in Luxembourg is mostly good.
@distractor-lu Wanter
@distractor-lu seelen
@distractor-en winter
@distractor-en rarely

@sentence
@lu Ech benotzen eng Sonnecrème, well ech séier e Sonnebrand kréien.
@en I use a suncream because I quickly get a sunburn.
@distractor-lu Sonnenhutt
@distractor-lu lues
@distractor-en hat
@distractor-en slowly
